+## Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=barryclark%2Fjekyll-now)
+
+The included `Anybuild` file tells Wasmer to install Jekyll, add the `jekyll-feed` and `jekyll-sitemap` plugins listed in `_config.yml`, run `jekyll build` and serve the `_site` folder, so `/feed.xml` and `/sitemap.xml` are generated. The button opens Wasmer's import page for this public repository, where you review the detected settings (and correct them if needed) before clicking Deploy; nothing is deployed until you do. It does not create a copy of the repository in your GitHub account; to deploy your own blog, fork Jekyll Now, edit `_config.yml` and your posts, and import your fork instead.
+
 ## Moar!
 
 I've created a more detailed walkthrough, [**Build A Blog With Jekyll And GitHub Pages**](http://www.smashingmagazine.com/2014/08/01/build-blog-jekyll-github-pages/) over at the Smashing Magazine website. Check it out if you'd like a more detailed walkthrough and some background on Jekyll. :metal:
